course: dictionary
lesson: 3737
title: Floppy and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Floppy describes things that are soft and hang down loosely, not stiff. You can see it in everyday things: a dog's ears, a sun hat, a rabbit's ears. The context shows the meaning: «a dog with floppy ears» tells you the ears hang down softly.
explain: Floppy has a second meaning too: weak and limp. «A floppy plant needs water» means the plant has gone droopy and weak, not stiff and upright. To check, swap in a word like limp or droopy and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Read the words around floppy to find which meaning fits. Ears and hats are soft and hang down. A plant that lacks water is weak. In health, a child who goes floppy and very sleepy is a serious warning sign, so you must get help at once.
fact: Floppy means soft and hanging down loosely, not stiff.
fact: Floppy can also mean weak and limp, like a plant that needs water.
fact: Floppy is an adjective, and its forms are floppier and floppiest.
fact: A floppy sun hat is soft and hangs down, and it shades your face and neck from the sun.
fact: If a baby or child suddenly goes floppy, get a doctor or emergency help straight away.
exercise: «The dog has floppy ears.» What does floppy mean here? | Wet and very cold | Stiff and pointing straight up | Loud and noisy | *Soft and hanging down loosely
exercise: «The plant looked floppy and sad, so Ella gave it a drink.» What was wrong with the plant? | It had too much water and was too strong | It was too tall to see | It was made of plastic | *It needed water and looked weak
exercise: «Male proboscis monkeys have a long floppy nose.» What does floppy suggest about the nose? | *It is soft and hangs down | It is painted bright red | It is very short | It is stiff and straight
test: «A floppy hat shades your face from the sun.» What does floppy mean in this sentence? | Hard and shiny | *Soft and hanging down loosely | Stuck firmly to the head | Rolled up tight
test: Sam says floppy only means loud. Why is Sam wrong? | Floppy is a word for a colour | Floppy means a loud noise from a dog | Floppy means loud, as the sentence shows | *Floppy means soft, hanging loosely, or weak, and it is not about loudness
exam: Read: «A child who is floppy and very sleepy needs help at once.» What does this teach you about floppy? | Floppy only ever describes soft hats | Floppy means very fast | *Floppy can mean weak and limp, and in a child it is a sign to get help at once | Floppy means very happy and full of energy
